	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg31225"></a>
		<table width="100%" cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" style="table-layout: fixed;">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="16%" rowspan="2" style="overflow: hidden;">
							<b><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?action=profile;u=1977" title="View the profile of djcoalesce">djcoalesce</a></b>
							<div class="smalltext">
								Newbie<br />
								<img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 4<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?action=profile;u=1977"><img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:djcoalesce@gmail.com"><img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</div>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=2634.msg31225#msg31225"><img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=2634.msg31225#msg31225">Re: More on the WAR AGAINST IMMIGRANTS</a></b>
									<div class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #1 on:</b> June 15, 2007, 02:00:29 am &#187;</div></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;">When more accountability from private enterprise is asked by the American people concerning immigration, it seems that corporations are quick to point out that cheaper prices have a consequence.&nbsp; Exploitation of cheap labor being an important factor in this &quot;consequence of consumerism&quot;. Let&#039;s stop supporting businesses that use illegal labor.&nbsp; <br />Let&#039;s start forcing businesses to think of more creative solutions for our labor shortage. A solution that is legal and will not break any laws.&nbsp; <br />For instance, the farming industry can mechanize more so there will be no need for back breaking labor.&nbsp; Also, the way we build homes is very inefficient.&nbsp; The process can be changed to reduce labor costs and more importantly, keep prices low for the &quot;American consumerist&quot;.&nbsp; Check out the way Quadrant Homes does it.&nbsp; I heard on NPR that because of a labor shortage during the past few seasons, farmers are actually looking into more ways to rely less on manual labor (migrant workers) by mechanizing.&nbsp; <br />This article illustrates what the government should do to keep the trust of the American people. It also reminds businesses that they cannot exploit cheap labor and refuse to innovate just because they don&#039;t want to invest the time and money.&nbsp; </div>
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext" width="85%">
							<table width="100%" border="0" style="table-layout: fixed;"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext" width="100%">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" />
									Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg31876"></a>
		<table width="100%" cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" style="table-layout: fixed;">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="16%" rowspan="2" style="overflow: hidden;">
							<b><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?action=profile;u=716" title="View the profile of CoolPapaBrown">CoolPapaBrown</a></b>
							<div class="smalltext">
								Newbie<br />
								<img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 11<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?action=profile;u=716"><img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</div>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=2634.msg31876#msg31876"><img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=2634.msg31876#msg31876">Re: More on the WAR AGAINST IMMIGRANTS</a></b>
									<div class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #2 on:</b> June 20, 2007, 10:53:24 am &#187;</div></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;">DjCoalesce, I disagree with the focus of your response. First, we must stop referring to immigrants as &quot;cheap labor.&quot; They are more than this. That article is about peoples&#039; lives being destroyed. Something that we forget. Undocumented immigrants are human beings.<br /><br />This article is not just about keeping &quot;the trust of the American people.&quot; By violating the basic human rights of immigrants (as occurs regularly through the detention process), my trust has been broken. It&#039;s about &quot;us&quot; as human beings. Not as Americans. (BTW, I don&#039;t know if everyone on this board is &quot;American&quot; or necessarily has papers.)<br /><br />Regarding laws being broken, that&#039;s partially the result of not enough visas being allotted for jobs that clearly need more workers. Further mechanizing the industry is one thing, but until that happens, people are needed. Fair immigration policy that allows workers to come north and potentially bring their families is humane.<br /><br />How about we talk about trade policies, like NAFTA, that sent tons of cheap grain from American agrobusinesses to Mexico destroying small Mexican farms. Also, putting many people (and whole towns) out of work forcing them to travel up north. <br /><br />Furthermore, I used the word &quot;war&quot; intentionally. Immigration is under the department of Homeland Security. How not giving immigrants their fair day in court or due process is &quot;strengthening our borders&quot; or &quot;protecting democracy&quot; is beyond me. <br /><br />I agree that business needs to be more accountable, but the issue is bigger than that. It&#039;s MUCH MORE IMPORTANT than keeping &quot;prices low for the &quot;American consumerist.&quot;<br /><br />When we think about the debate SOLELY in terms of economics, we make it an &quot;us vs. them&quot; debate. Those with the privilege of status, and those without. <br /><br />SIDENOTE: Please everyone, no more use of the word &quot;illegal.&quot; Use &quot;undocumented.&quot; People are NOT born &quot;illegal.&quot; It is the result of legislation and inequality of power. <br /><br /></div>
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext" width="85%">
